{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/895040-more-methods-for-mortals-to-resist-contest-supernatural-powers","id":895040,"title":"More Methods For Mortals To Resist/Contest Supernatural Powers?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-20T15:23:35-07:00","id":895040,"title":"More Methods For Mortals To Resist/Contest Supernatural Powers?","content":"I want to see if I know all the official methods and alternate interpretations. If you have written any relevant Merits or house rules, please share them.<br /> <br /> We have Indomitable as the most direct example, but Closed Book can help against mind-reading at ST discretion. Meditative Mind 2 gives a +3 bonus to any Resolve + Composure made on the same day you meditated, but we can house rule it to also give +2 on rolls to contest supernatural mind/emotion control. Hardy gives +1 to +3 to any rolls to resist disease, poison, deprivation, unconsciousness or deprivation. This can be house ruled so it also applies to rolls to contest supernatural powers to alter your body. Every dot of Integrity above 7 gives +1 for Abjurations, but we can come up with a 2 dot Merit that can apply said bonus to contest other supernatural powers.<br /> <br /> However, there should be a limit so that mortals will not stack all of that to have higher dice pools than the majority of supernaturals. A mortal with Resolve 3, Composure 3, Meditative Mind 2, Integrity 8, Conviction 3 (which gives +2) and who spends a Willpower point to contest mind or emotion-affecting powers would roll 10 dice. My hunch is to say that bonuses from Merits cap at +5, but Conviction and Willpower expenditure may take it higher. But even then, mortals would still have big enough dice pools to reliably confront all but the most powerful supernaturals. And that's without going into Advanced and Epic Merits.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T04:59:27-07:00","id":895423,"title":"","content":"Conviction? I don't know what that is.<br /> <br /> Either way, while there's a lot of stuff here for anti-vampire (lots of mind control in that game)? Pretty much we're looking at a lack of anti-anyone else. Werewolves have a host of powers that don't rely on direct mind effects or are resisted in that fashion. Mages flat out ignore everything but direct boosts to Resolve, Stamina and Composure. Changelings have a number of abilities that are contested, but a large number of these contested effects manipulate a target's luck, time or senses, of which none of your house rules touch. Demonic Embeds and many Demon Form abilities ignore reistances. Nightmares likely can be resisted, but not Atavisms nor invoking Lair traits. <br /> <br /> There is also a problem with your attempt to use Integrity - even a homebrew merit is likely to fail, because it implies constant exposure to the supernatural. Constant exposure to the supernatural degrades one's Integrity. Its a losing proposition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T10:28:57-07:00","id":895547,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MCN</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/895040-more-methods-for-mortals-to-resist-contest-supernatural-powers?p=895423#post895423\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Conviction? I don't know what that is.<br /> <br /> Either way, while there's a lot of stuff here for anti-vampire (lots of mind control in that game)? Pretty much we're looking at a lack of anti-anyone else. Werewolves have a host of powers that don't rely on direct mind effects or are resisted in that fashion. Mages flat out ignore everything but direct boosts to Resolve, Stamina and Composure. Changelings have a number of abilities that are contested, but a large number of these contested effects manipulate a target's luck, time or senses, of which none of your house rules touch. Demonic Embeds and many Demon Form abilities ignore reistances. Nightmares likely can be resisted, but not Atavisms nor invoking Lair traits.<br /> <br /> There is also a problem with your attempt to use Integrity - even a homebrew merit is likely to fail, because it implies constant exposure to the supernatural. Constant exposure to the supernatural degrades one's Integrity. Its a losing proposition.</div> </div> </div> </div> Conviction is a &quot;Powerstat&quot; for mortals from the Mirrors supplement in 1ED. Besides offering a Supernatural Tolerance, it can be used to spend multiple Willpower points per turn for different effects, which goes well with Risking Willpower and other Hunter mechanics.<br /> <br /> Your observations about non-vampiric powers are spot-on, especially the one about Integrity. I could hack the setting so that supernatural powers are always resisted or contested, but they come from such wildly different sources that it wouldn't make metaphysical sense. Perhaps a Supernatural Style? Regardless of how a mortal might get that, they'd lose it after acquiring a major template, same as other supernatural Merits. If I write up this Supernatural Style, I'll try to focus on bonuses other than just extra dice.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Bye.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4443-gibberingeloquence","name":"GibberingEloquence","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4443_5.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2470"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-21T15:53:15-07:00","id":895720,"title":"","content":"Personally, I suggest waiting for HtV. That game is built to handle this kind of thing, while core mortal is not; there may be further suggestions or merits there. Or just remake the Supernatural Tolerance merit from Second Sight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2102-mcn","name":"MCN","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2102_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3479"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-22T05:53:07-07:00","id":896031,"title":"","content":"I would say look <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1X_eASK_Zmfa9rvbrw0RR56iHvVNSCEoxOqTDiQWnWyY/edit?pref=2&amp;pli=1#heading=h.301hkb4eklhm\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.<br /> <br /> The playtest for Psychic Vampire in Hurt Locker has a general &quot;Supernatural Resistance&quot; merit that allows a mortal touched by the supernatural to gain supernatural tolerance. It is an elegant solution for mortals that are quasi supernatural. You may expand its use for veteran hunters or just hand out a few dots to the players as a freebie.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1420009-the-artificer-s-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">The Artificer's Workshop</a> - A collection of Exalted Artifacts<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806809-curios-relics-and-tomes\" target=\"_blank\">Curios, Relics, and Tomes</a> - A collection of Relics (Cursed and Otherwise)<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/793173-the-horror-show\" target=\"_blank\">The Horror Lab</a> - A collection of Beasts, Monsters and less definable things.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1128197-strange-places#post1128197\" target=\"_blank\">Strange Places</a> - A collection of Dark, Mysterious, and Wondrous Locations<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/993181-twilight-menagerie\" target=\"_blank\">Twilight Menagerie</a> - A collection of Ephemeral Entities","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/775-reighnhell","name":"Reighnhell","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar775_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"749"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}